{"availability":"available","full":"gobelinor/stem-extractor","name":"stem-extractor","description":"Extract per-track WAV stems from hardware music machines (OP-XY) via MIDI solo + audio recording. Browser-based, framework-agnostic engine.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":7,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-31T12:53:14Z","updated":"2026-09-11T03:10:34Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://stem-extractor.pages.dev/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:32.813Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:32.813Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:32.813Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T08:58:32.813Z","stars":7,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Pull aligned per-track WAV stems out of your hardware — straight from the browser.","Grooveboxes only send a stereo master over USB — no multitrack out. So getting stems means soloing each track by hand, recording, and repeating. Stem Extractor automates it: it solos each track over MIDI, records the stereo output, and gives you one sample-aligned WAV per track — drop them into your DAW and they're in time.","OP-XY only for now. Other machines are one file to add — request one."],"features":["🎚️ Automated solo + record, one track at a time","🎯 Sample-aligned (the app drives the MIDI clock)","🔒 Runs in your browser, audio stays local, no signup"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/gobelinor/stem-extractor/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7ce460932dec59b112381e825b046c3e46e599ba5c7b2a2358d9e1ccf1bf1806","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:33.066Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:33.066Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Pull aligned per-track WAV stems out of your hardware — straight from the browser.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/gobelinor/stem-extractor/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"7ce460932dec59b112381e825b046c3e46e599ba5c7b2a23